say "Free services sleep after 15 idle minutes (~60s wake). A visitor's scan"
say "or a Telnyx webhook must never eat that — so ping the APP service only."
open_url "https://uptimerobot.com"
step "Create a free account -> Add New Monitor -> HTTP(s):"
say  "    URL:      https://${APP_SERVICE}.onrender.com/auth/signin"
say  "    Interval: 5 minutes"
step "(Delete this monitor after the event — it's what spends instance hours.)"
pause "Press Enter once the monitor is up..."
say ""
say "The QR code IS the sign-in. It must encode EXACTLY this URL (the app"
say "host — the console host would land visitors signed out):"
say ""
say "    ${DEMO_URL}"
say ""
if command -v qrencode >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  qrencode -t ANSIUTF8 "$DEMO_URL" || true
  say "(also saving demo-qr.png next to this script)"
  qrencode -o scripts/demo-qr.png -s 10 "$DEMO_URL" || true
else
  step "qrencode isn't installed — generate the QR at a generator you trust"
  step "(the URL contains the access code) and print it big for the pitch."
fi
note "Leak plan: if the code escapes early, change DEMO_ACCESS_CODE on the"
note "app service's env in Render — it auto-redeploys and old QRs die."

# ── Stage 13 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
stage "Demo-day smoke test + the day after"
say "The full visitor journey, on your own phone, before you pitch:"
step "Scan the QR -> you land signed in on the Becca Demo overview."
step "Open an example agent -> Test -> enter YOUR number -> phone rings ->"
step "have the conversation -> transcript + extracted answers appear."
step "Open Launch: the button is disabled with a 'blocking' pill — intended."
step "(That's the pre-flight safety gate; visitors can see it, never fire it.)"
step "Billing: the wallet visibly debited for your test call."
say ""
say "The day after the demo:"
step "Blank DEMO_ACCESS_CODE on the app service env (route vanishes on the"
step "auto-redeploy); rotate SESSION_SECRET to kill any 14-day cookies."
step "Delete the UptimeRobot monitor."
step "pg_dump anything you want to keep — the free DB expires 30 days after"
step "creation."
step "Delete the two services + database in Render when done."
pause "Press Enter to finish..."

finish
say "Re-run any time: bash scripts/demo-wizard.sh — it remembers .env.demo."
say "Mid-demo wallet refill:"
say "  DATABASE_URL=<External URL> uv run python scripts/seed_demo.py --email ${DEMO_USER_EMAIL} --credit 40"
